Toast creates technology to help restaurants and local businesses succeed in a digital world, helping business owners operate, increase sales, engage customers, and keep employees happy.

We are seeking a Senior Payroll Specialist to join our in-house North America (NAM) payroll team. This is a high-impact, hybrid role that owns the most complex payroll processing, escalations, and systems and compliance initiatives, while overseeing and reviewing the day-to-day transactional work delivered by the Payroll&nbsp; team. As part of Toast’s internal payroll organization - not a third-party payroll bureau or outsourced provider - you will act as a subject-matter expert across payroll operations, compliance, and systems; mentor Payroll Specialists and help prepare them for advancement; and serve as a key backup to the Payroll Team Lead. Based in India, this position supports payroll for employees in the NAM region; it does not involve India payroll processing.&nbsp;

A day in the life (Responsibilities)&nbsp;

• Payroll Operations &amp; Volume: Oversee accurate and timely processing of bi-weekly multi-state payrolls for more than 5,700 employees across the US, Canada, and Mexico, with day-to-day transaction processing primarily executed by the Payroll Specialist team. Personally owns and processes the most complex, escalated, and Mexico payroll cycles.&nbsp;

• Complex Transactions &amp; Global Mobility: Own complex and escalated payroll transactions that fall outside standard Specialist-level processing, including benefits-in-kind processing and overpayment calculations and repayments. Coordinate with third-party consultants and Global Mobility to input transferred employees' payroll information accurately and in a timely manner.&nbsp;

• Employee Ticketing &amp; Tier 2 Support: Support our internal and external customers who have payroll inquiries. Manage and respond to ServiceNow tickets accurately on the first instance. Proactively ensure all errors and issues are being resolved as indicated in the Service Level Agreement (SLA).&nbsp;

• System &amp; Data Management: Ensure Workday is maintained as the primary source of data integrity. Responsible for Workday EIB (Enterprise Interface Builder) mass data uploads, global mobility transactions, and serving as the lead tester for User Acceptance Testing (UAT) and semi-annual Workday system releases.&nbsp;

• Reporting &amp; General Ledger: Review and analyze payroll and data analysis reports - including those generated by the Payroll Specialist team - to ensure audits are completed accurately and on time. Maintain and reconcile General Ledger accounts, ensuring accounts are balanced. Create content for dashboards and metrics as needed.&nbsp;

• Compliance, SOX &amp; Audits: Work with the Payroll Team Lead on quarterly reviews of the SOX (Sarbanes-Oxley) payroll process and support Internal Audit requirements. Manage audits for 401K (US retirement savings plans), ESPP, Workers' Compensation, and review/approve monthly, quarterly, and annual equity audits. Review annual tax statements (W-2’s, T4’s) for all expatriate personnel to ensure accuracy.&nbsp;

• Vendor Management &amp; Tax Filings: Coordinate with ADP SmartCompliance and CloudPay on tax filings, notice resolutions, and reconciliations. Own ADP tax-registration administration, including applying for new SIT, SUI, and local tax IDs and maintaining accurate payroll tax records. Process Prior Quarter/Prior Year Tax adjustments as needed. Manage responses to all tax agency inquiries through ADP Tax Service and CloudPay.&nbsp;

• Process Improvement &amp; Troubleshooting: Audit current processes to reduce the number of payroll-related errors. Determine the root cause of payroll errors by collecting and analyzing information under strict deadlines. Assist with the development and final review of payroll policies, workflows, knowledge bases, and contingency plans. Maintain and update Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) documentation,

CLEAR is building THE secure identity company of the future. Our mission is to make experiences safer and easier-physically and digitally. With more than 43 million Members and a growing network of partners across the world, CLEAR's secure identity platform is transforming the way people live, work, and travel. Whether it’s at the airport, stadium, or throughout your everyday life, CLEAR unlocks the magic of frictionless experiences.

The Senior Accountant will play a key role in CLEAR’s financial close and reporting processes, ensuring accurate financial records, strong internal controls, and compliance with U.S. GAAP. You’ll own complex accounting activities, partner across the business to resolve challenges, and drive improvements through automation, AI, and scalable accounting processes.

&nbsp;

What you'll do:

• Own key general ledger activities across monthly, quarterly, and annual close cycles, ensuring accuracy, timeliness, and accountability&nbsp;

• Prepare and review journal entries, balance sheet reconciliations, and flux analyses across areas including fixed assets, prepaid expenses, accruals, payroll, cash, and investments&nbsp;

• Partner with Finance, Payroll, Legal, and Operations to resolve complex accounting matters and support financial reporting and audit requests&nbsp;

• Execute and strengthen internal controls, maintaining SOX compliance and clear, audit-ready documentation • Identify and implement process improvements, leveraging AI, automation, and system enhancements to streamline workflows and increase efficiency

&nbsp;

How you'll measure success:

• Timely and accurate completion of assigned monthly, quarterly, and annual close activities • Reduction in reconciliation discrepancies, adjusting entries, and unresolved accounting items&nbsp;

• Consistent execution of SOX controls and timely resolution of audit requests and findings&nbsp;

• Measurable improvements in close efficiency, process automation, and reporting accuracy

&nbsp;

What you're great at:

• 5+ years of progressive accounting experience with strong U.S. GAAP knowledge and experience managing complex general ledger activities; public accounting experience preferred&nbsp;

• Strong understanding of SOX controls, financial reporting, accounting systems, and technical accounting principles&nbsp;

• Independently navigating complex accounting matters, exercising sound judgment, and solving problems without established processes or templates&nbsp;

• Building trusted cross-functional relationships and communicating financial information clearly to accounting and non-accounting stakeholders&nbsp;

• Driving continuous improvement through analytical thinking, strong organization, and curiosity about AI, automation, and emerging technologies

&nbsp;

How You'll be Rewarded:

At CLEAR, we help YOU move forward - because when you’re at your best, we’re at our best. You’ll work with talented team members motivated by our mission of making experiences safer and easier. Our offices are bright and energetic with an open concept and plenty of conference rooms and casual co-working spaces. We also offer catered lunches every day and have fully stocked kitchens. Outside of the office, we invest in your well-being and learning &amp; development with stipends and reimbursement programs.&nbsp;

We offer holistic total rewards, including comprehensive healthcare plans, family-building benefits (fertility and adoption/surrogacy support), flexible time off, annual wellness stipend, free OneMedical memberships for you and your dependents, a CLEAR Plus membership, and a 401(k) retirement plan with employer match. The base salary range for this role is $130,000.00 - $155,000.00, depending on levels of skills and experience.

